WEBVTT

00:00:41.670 --> 00:00:42.947
Hey,  Maddie.

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:45.436
Listen, I, uh, hate to pull you away,

00:00:45.439 --> 00:00:48.123
But I'm gonna need you to come
back to the office with me.

00:00:48.161 --> 00:00:49.727
Really?

00:00:49.730 --> 00:00:53.627
Yeah, it turns out I got to
file those docs by midnight.

00:00:53.630 --> 00:00:57.177
I'm gonna need you to, um...

00:00:59.620 --> 00:01:01.587
This isn't working at all, is it?

00:01:01.590 --> 00:01:03.057
No, it's not, Nate.

00:01:03.060 --> 00:01:04.227
Listen, I've had a couple.

00:01:04.430 --> 00:01:06.107
I shouldn't really drive.

00:01:06.410 --> 00:01:09.137
Could you just give me a lift
--  I already called you a cab.

00:01:10.760 --> 00:01:12.517
I'll see you in the morning.

00:01:20.230 --> 00:01:21.557
Does that happen a lot?

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:23.867
Only on the days that end with a Y.

00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:35.607
You okay?

00:01:36.850 --> 00:01:37.827
Yeah.

00:01:41.570 --> 00:01:42.867
I've got to go.

00:03:39.610 --> 00:03:41.327
Here is the detective

00:03:48.230 --> 00:03:49.547
That's a pretty nasty bite.

00:03:50.350 --> 00:03:51.457
You know what bit him?

00:03:51.460 --> 00:03:54.167
I haven't quite
determined that just yet.

00:03:55.650 --> 00:03:56.657
Come on, doc.

00:03:56.660 --> 00:03:58.057
Off the record.

00:03:58.870 --> 00:04:02.227
Okay, way, way off the record.

00:04:02.820 --> 00:04:06.337
If I didn't know better, I'd say
the guy was attacked by a wolf.

00:04:06.340 --> 00:04:10.117
But unless I know that the zoo is missing
one of their lobos, I'm going with pit bull.

00:04:10.120 --> 00:04:11.787
I like my job.

00:04:11.790 --> 00:04:12.977
Yeah, I hear you.

00:04:12.980 --> 00:04:13.977
One more thing.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:16.777
This guy -Was his heart missing?

00:04:17.890 --> 00:04:19.107
Yeah, how did you know that?

00:04:19.110 --> 00:04:20.637
I haven't even finished my report.

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:22.157
Lucky guess.

00:04:26.500 --> 00:04:29.017
This lawyer guy first
heart-Free corpse in town?

00:04:29.020 --> 00:04:30.277
First man.

00:04:30.550 --> 00:04:32.707
Over the past year, several
women have gone missing.

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:38.107
Dead bodies all washed up later in the bay,
too deteriorated to draw firm conclusions.

00:04:38.110 --> 00:04:40.357
But no hearts. No hearts

00:04:40.400 --> 00:04:42.117
They were all hookers
working at hunter's point.

00:04:42.120 --> 00:04:43.912
Cops are trying to
keep things under wrap,

00:04:43.915 --> 00:04:47.527
But they're looking for a serial
killer. And the lunar cycle?

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:50.927
Yeah, month after month, all the murders
happened in the week leading up to the full moon.

00:04:50.930 --> 00:04:53.197
Which is this week. There is the lawer

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:54.447
Awesome.

00:04:55.800 --> 00:04:57.987
Dean, could you be a
bigger geek about this?

00:04:57.990 --> 00:05:00.231
I'm sorry, man, but what
about a human by day,

00:05:00.234 --> 00:05:03.269
A freak animal killing machine
by moonlight don't you understand?

00:05:03.272 --> 00:05:06.914
We haven't seen one since we were kids.

00:05:07.140 --> 00:05:08.407
Okay, sparky.

00:05:08.720 --> 00:05:09.707
Then you know what?

00:05:09.710 --> 00:05:12.842
After we kill it, we can go to disneyland.
Know what the best part about it is?

00:05:12.845 --> 00:05:16.965
We already know how to
bring these suckers down.

00:05:17.660 --> 00:05:18.867
So what's our next move?

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:20.717
Talk to the girl who found the body.

00:05:22.490 --> 00:05:23.507
Madison: I don't understand.

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:24.947
I already gave my statement to you.

00:05:24.950 --> 00:05:27.427
Well, we just need to
verify a few things.

00:05:27.430 --> 00:05:30.627
This is my neighbor glenn.
Glenn, this is detective...

00:05:30.630 --> 00:05:32.913
Landis. And detective dante.

00:05:32.951 --> 00:05:35.087
Well, guess I'll leave you to it.

00:05:37.914 --> 00:05:38.628
Okay.

00:05:38.631 --> 00:05:40.087
Thanks for the casserole.

00:05:41.160 --> 00:05:42.327
Oh, how thoughtful.

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:44.517
Just call if you need anything.

00:05:47.150 --> 00:05:48.027
He's sweet.

00:05:48.030 --> 00:05:49.927
He came over to check on me.

00:05:50.450 --> 00:05:52.177
Have a seat.

00:05:57.900 --> 00:05:59.637
You must be pretty shaken up.

00:06:00.320 --> 00:06:02.307
You were nate mulligan's
assistant, right?

00:06:02.310 --> 00:06:03.307
For two years, yeah.

00:06:03.310 --> 00:06:04.997
So you knew all about him.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:07.287
Probably knew more
about him than he did.

00:06:07.290 --> 00:06:08.297
Nate was...

00:06:08.660 --> 00:06:09.907
He was nice.

00:06:11.040 --> 00:06:13.287
But...

00:06:13.290 --> 00:06:16.711
You get a few scotches in him, and he
started hitting on anyone in a 5-Miles radius.

00:06:16.714 --> 00:06:18.657
You know the type.

00:06:22.330 --> 00:06:25.067
Yeah. I do, actually.

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:28.367
Did, uh, did he have any
enemies? What do you mean?

00:06:28.370 --> 00:06:30.164
Sure looked like an animal attack.

00:06:30.167 --> 00:06:32.417
We're just covering all the bases.

00:06:32.420 --> 00:06:33.640
Anyone that might have
had a beef with him

00:06:33.643 --> 00:06:36.388
Former client, an ex. What?

00:06:36.391 --> 00:06:38.045
Well, this is embarrassing,

00:06:38.048 --> 00:06:39.773
But my ex-Boyfriend, kurt.

00:06:39.776 --> 00:06:41.340
Kurt have a last name? Mueller

00:06:41.378 --> 00:06:43.287
After we broke up, he went kind of nuts.

00:06:43.290 --> 00:06:44.447
He's...

00:06:44.790 --> 00:06:46.867
Well, he's kind of been stalking me.

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:50.077
He got it in his head that something
was going on between Nate and I.

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:51.667
He showed up at my office.

00:06:51.670 --> 00:06:53.484
And what happened? Kurt
got into it with nate.

00:06:53.487 --> 00:06:56.456
Threw a punch before security grabbed
him. I was lucky to keep my job.

00:06:56.459 --> 00:06:57.717
When was the last time you saw kurt?

00:06:57.720 --> 00:06:58.817
A few nights ago.

00:06:58.820 --> 00:07:00.487
Actually, the night Nate died.

00:07:00.490 --> 00:07:03.277
We were all grabbing drinks at
this bar, and Kurt showed up.

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:04.117
And?

00:07:04.120 --> 00:07:05.037
Nothing.

00:07:05.640 --> 00:07:06.637
It was...

00:07:06.640 --> 00:07:08.677
Like he was watching me.

00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:10.167
Then he was gone.

00:07:10.170 --> 00:07:11.597
Tell you the truth...

00:07:12.290 --> 00:07:13.957
He scares me.

00:07:16.540 --> 00:07:17.717
So, what do you think?

00:07:17.720 --> 00:07:19.797
Stalker ex-Boyfriend.

00:07:19.800 --> 00:07:21.037
He hates the boss.

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:22.287
And he was there that night.

00:07:22.290 --> 00:07:23.687
Think he's our dog-Faced boy?

00:07:23.950 --> 00:07:25.827
Well, it's a theory.

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:27.777
We've had worse.

00:07:28.400 --> 00:07:30.947
What do you say we pay kurt a visit?

00:08:56.500 --> 00:08:58.967
Nothing but leftovers and a six-Pack.

00:08:59.450 --> 00:09:00.677
Check the freezer.

00:09:00.680 --> 00:09:04.057
Maybe there's some human hearts
behind the haagen-Dazs or something.

00:09:30.280 --> 00:09:31.507
Sam, come here.

00:09:37.000 --> 00:09:38.337
Check it out.

00:09:50.020 --> 00:09:51.347
Somebody there?

00:10:22.600 --> 00:10:24.387
I'll call 911.

00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:34.777
I'd say Kurt's looking
more and more like our cujo.

00:10:34.780 --> 00:10:37.737
If he's out here, we
better check on Madison.

00:10:42.480 --> 00:10:43.497
What's going on?

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:45.517
Police business, glenn.

00:10:47.460 --> 00:10:48.677
What is it?

00:10:50.560 --> 00:10:53.077
Well, maybe we should talk privately?

00:10:53.700 --> 00:10:55.267
Has kurt been here?

00:10:55.270 --> 00:10:57.007
Not exactly.

00:10:57.450 --> 00:11:00.087
What exactly does "not exactly" mean?

00:11:00.090 --> 00:11:04.377
Well, he was outside
last night -Just looking.

00:11:04.380 --> 00:11:06.617
Just looking at me.

00:11:07.000 --> 00:11:08.697
Has he done something?

00:11:08.700 --> 00:11:11.347
We're not really sure.
It's probably nothing.

00:11:11.350 --> 00:11:12.427
But...

00:11:12.430 --> 00:11:13.767
We just don't want to take any chances.

00:11:13.770 --> 00:11:15.939
In fact, one of us should
probably stay here with you,

00:11:15.942 --> 00:11:17.669
Just in case he stops by.

00:11:17.950 --> 00:11:20.297
Where does he work? He owns a body shop.

00:11:20.433 --> 00:11:23.217
You mind grabbing that
address for us? Thanks.

00:11:25.070 --> 00:11:28.107
All right, you go.I'll stay.
You go after the creepy ex.

00:11:28.110 --> 00:11:29.407
I'm gonna hang here with the hot chick.

00:11:29.410 --> 00:11:31.637
Why do you always get to
hang out with the girls?

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:33.067
Because I'm older.

00:11:33.640 --> 00:11:36.627
No, screw that. We settle
this the old-Fashioned way.

00:11:42.940 --> 00:11:44.797
Dean, always with the scissors.

00:11:44.800 --> 00:11:47.227
Shut up. Shut up. Two out of three.

00:11:51.260 --> 00:11:51.660
God!

00:11:51.760 --> 00:11:53.447
Bundle up out there, all right?

00:12:15.240 --> 00:12:18.037
Um, do you want to sit on the
couch? No. No, no, I'm okay.

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:20.797
It's more comfortable. Uh, I'm fine.

00:12:41.280 --> 00:12:43.967
You know, I think I
will sit on the couch.

00:12:57.690 --> 00:12:59.107
Let me guess.

00:12:59.110 --> 00:13:02.095
You're sitting on her couch trying
to think of something to say.

00:13:02.098 --> 00:13:03.823
Did you find kurt? He
hasn't been at work all week,

00:13:03.826 --> 00:13:07.029
But because I'm good, and
I mean really, really good,

00:13:07.032 --> 00:13:09.847
I got a line on where he might be.

00:13:11.770 --> 00:13:14.467
What's she wearing? Bye, dean.

00:13:17.490 --> 00:13:19.237
Oh, sammy.

00:13:29.900 --> 00:13:32.717
Who died and made you sheriff?
I will call who I want.

00:13:32.920 --> 00:13:36.457
Whatever you want. Look what time it is.

00:13:36.460 --> 00:13:39.347
You're gonna wake her up and start talking about
- I saw that.

00:13:39.350 --> 00:13:41.217
What? Saw what?

00:13:41.460 --> 00:13:42.793
Okay, this
is the deal --

00:13:42.796 --> 00:13:46.097
My house, my tv.

00:13:46.100 --> 00:13:48.254
I never get to watch my show,

00:13:48.257 --> 00:13:50.092
So suck it up.

00:14:02.510 --> 00:14:03.462
Wait, so

00:14:03.465 --> 00:14:07.691
So kindall married ethan's
father just to get back at him?

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:11.227
And now she's set to inherit all the
casinos that were supposed to go to ethan.

00:14:11.230 --> 00:14:13.597
What a bitch!

00:14:16.180 --> 00:14:18.957
Admit it -You're hooked.
No, no, no, no, no, no.

00:14:18.960 --> 00:14:21.467
I wouldn't say I'm hooked.

00:14:24.690 --> 00:14:26.407
Can I ask you a question?

00:14:26.650 --> 00:14:29.617
It's ... it's a little personal.

00:14:29.620 --> 00:14:31.917
You've seen my entire
underwear collection.

00:14:31.920 --> 00:14:34.217
Go ahead.

00:14:34.220 --> 00:14:35.997
Okay, um...

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:39.627
Well, you're -You're clearly smart.

00:14:39.630 --> 00:14:42.557
I mean, your house is full
of great books, you know?

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:45.957
And you're independent. Uh-Huh.

00:14:46.950 --> 00:14:49.987
What were you doing with kurt?

00:14:51.530 --> 00:14:53.367
I don't know.

00:14:54.320 --> 00:14:56.281
I mean, it's not like he
introduced himself, like,

00:14:56.284 --> 00:14:59.050
Hi, I'm possessive and controlling,
and I like to punch people.

00:14:59.053 --> 00:15:01.826
Want to be my girlfriend?

00:15:01.829 --> 00:15:03.065
Yeah, well,

00:15:03.068 --> 00:15:04.841
I guess we all make mistakes.

00:15:04.844 --> 00:15:07.527
Yeah, well, mine's wanted by the police.

00:15:08.170 --> 00:15:11.257
You want to know why I
stayed with him? Really?

00:15:12.880 --> 00:15:14.917
I was too insecure to leave.

00:15:14.920 --> 00:15:18.267
Well, I find that hard to believe.
You don't really seem like the type.

00:15:18.270 --> 00:15:20.427
Yeah, well some stuff happened.

00:15:20.860 --> 00:15:23.397
My life changed, I changed,
for the better, I think.

00:15:23.400 --> 00:15:26.717
What happened? Well, for
one thing, I got mugged.

00:15:27.650 --> 00:15:29.637
And that's supposed to be a good thing?

00:15:29.640 --> 00:15:31.342
I know, it sounds strange,

00:15:31.345 --> 00:15:32.802
And don't get me
wrong -It rattled me --

00:15:32.805 --> 00:15:35.031
But then it hit me.

00:15:35.034 --> 00:15:40.087
I could keep feeling sorry for myself
or I could take control of my life.

00:15:40.090 --> 00:15:42.197
I chose the latter.

00:15:42.850 --> 00:15:44.767
First thing I did was
tell kurt he had to go.

00:15:44.770 --> 00:15:48.047
Smart move. Apparently.

00:15:48.050 --> 00:15:51.027
Everything else just
opened up, blossomed.

00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:53.187
It's all been wonderful, really.

00:15:53.960 --> 00:15:55.347
What?

00:15:57.170 --> 00:15:59.341
Doesn't everybody think that being
a victim of random violence is

00:15:59.344 --> 00:16:01.465
The best thing that
ever happened to them?

00:16:01.490 --> 00:16:03.547
Yeah, not so much.

00:16:06.970 --> 00:16:08.867
You're...

00:16:08.870 --> 00:16:10.597
Unusual.

00:16:12.230 --> 00:16:14.237
Unusual like...

00:16:14.610 --> 00:16:17.157
"Unusual"? No, no, no.

00:16:17.160 --> 00:16:20.087
Unusual like...

00:16:22.900 --> 00:16:24.687
Impressive.

00:16:28.480 --> 00:16:29.797
You think so?

00:16:34.760 --> 00:16:36.127
Sorry.

00:16:39.450 --> 00:16:41.346
Hey. I found him.

00:16:41.400 --> 00:16:43.657
Good. Don't take your eyes off him.

00:16:47.340 --> 00:16:49.217
Oh, yeah, my eyes are glued.

00:16:49.220 --> 00:16:51.197
Look, sammy, I got to let you go.

00:16:51.200 --> 00:16:53.807
I, uh, I don't want to miss anything.

00:17:04.190 --> 00:17:05.777
So, um...

00:17:06.480 --> 00:17:07.887
I'm gonna turn in.

00:17:07.890 --> 00:17:08.847
Okay, yeah.

00:17:08.850 --> 00:17:11.107
Well, I'll be here. Okay.

00:17:11.110 --> 00:17:16.247
If you hear anything, if you
wake up, just -Just call out.

00:17:18.990 --> 00:17:21.767
Okay. Okay.

00:18:53.760 --> 00:18:56.807
Dean, you okay? Yeah,
now that I'm conscious.

00:18:56.810 --> 00:18:58.667
The werewolf knocked me out.

00:18:58.670 --> 00:19:00.157
Sam, it's madison.

00:19:00.160 --> 00:19:01.247
What? !

00:19:01.250 --> 00:19:03.797
Yeah, awesome job of
keeping an eye on her.

00:19:08.210 --> 00:19:11.037
Dean, I've been here the whole
time. She's in bed asleep.

00:19:11.040 --> 00:19:12.357
Well, she wasn't an hour ago.

00:19:12.360 --> 00:19:15.947
Check her right arm. I nicked
her with a silver knife.

00:19:18.330 --> 00:19:19.707
Morning.

00:19:27.060 --> 00:19:29.567
Um, wherare my pajamas?

00:19:32.450 --> 00:19:34.097
Sam?

00:19:34.100 --> 00:19:36.117
What's going on?

00:19:38.120 --> 00:19:40.237
Where are you going?

00:19:40.240 --> 00:19:42.257
I'm not going anywhere.

00:19:42.260 --> 00:19:44.707
And neither are you.

00:19:51.320 --> 00:19:52.607
You're psychotic.

00:19:52.610 --> 00:19:55.517
The whole "I'm a cop"
trick. God, I am so stupid.

00:19:55.520 --> 00:19:57.847
Well, I guess neither of us
are who we said we were, huh?

00:19:57.850 --> 00:19:59.307
Sam, you're sick, okay?

00:19:59.310 --> 00:20:00.707
You're imagining things.

00:20:00.710 --> 00:20:03.237
Monsters don't exist. Not really.

00:20:03.240 --> 00:20:05.607
You know what? Save the act.

00:20:05.610 --> 00:20:07.547
It's not an act!

00:20:07.550 --> 00:20:11.177
I am not a werewolf!
There is no such thing!

00:20:11.180 --> 00:20:13.587
It's made up, all right?

00:20:13.590 --> 00:20:15.797
They're not real! You
know they're not real!

00:20:15.800 --> 00:20:17.657
No? Then where did that come from?

00:20:17.660 --> 00:20:19.027
I don't know!

00:20:19.440 --> 00:20:22.057
Sam, god, you need help.

00:20:22.670 --> 00:20:25.107
Please, don't do something
that you're gonna regret.

00:20:25.110 --> 00:20:27.797
I'm not what you think I am.

00:20:27.800 --> 00:20:29.517
I'm not.

00:20:41.710 --> 00:20:43.447
How you doing?

00:20:44.720 --> 00:20:47.087
My head feels great, thanks.

00:20:47.900 --> 00:20:49.507
We got to talk.

00:20:55.460 --> 00:20:57.537
She says she has no idea
what I'm talking about.

00:20:57.540 --> 00:20:58.687
She's lying.

00:20:59.120 --> 00:21:00.793
Maybe. Or maybe she really
doesn't know she's changing.

00:21:00.796 --> 00:21:03.727
Maybe when the creature
takes over, she blacks out.

00:21:03.730 --> 00:21:05.617
Like a really hot incredible hulk?

00:21:05.620 --> 00:21:08.937
Dude, she ganked her boss and her ex-Boyfriend.
That doesn't sound ration unconscious.

00:21:08.940 --> 00:21:10.487
But what if it was, dean?

00:21:10.490 --> 00:21:13.907
What if some animal part of her
brain saw both those guys as threats?

00:21:13.910 --> 00:21:16.327
Hell, the cop, too. Are
you the dog whisperer now?

00:21:16.330 --> 00:21:18.157
Look, man, I just...

00:21:19.200 --> 00:21:21.549
I don't know. There was
something in her eyes.

00:21:21.552 --> 00:21:22.584
Yeah, she's killing people.

00:21:22.587 --> 00:21:25.160
But if she has no control..
Exactly she can't control it.

00:21:25.164 --> 00:21:27.156
Even if she's telling the truth,
it's not gonna change anything.

00:21:27.159 --> 00:21:29.575
I'm not putting a bullet through some
girl who has no idea what's happening.

00:21:29.578 --> 00:21:31.145
Sam she is master You're
feeling sorry for her?

00:21:31.148 --> 00:21:33.007
Maybe I understand her.

00:21:35.100 --> 00:21:39.567
Look, there might be another way we can get
the job done without having to waste her.

00:21:44.520 --> 00:21:46.797
Are you thinking what
I think you're thinking?

00:21:47.540 --> 00:21:48.767
Dad's theory.

00:21:48.770 --> 00:21:53.047
Lycanthropy might have a cure if you kill the
werewolf who bit you, severing the bloodline.

00:21:53.050 --> 00:21:55.067
Might have a cure. Meaning who knows?

00:21:55.070 --> 00:21:57.367
It's worth a shot.  We don't
even know where to look.

00:21:57.830 --> 00:22:01.267
The puppy that bit her -- It could be
anyone, anywhere. Could have been years ago.

00:22:03.520 --> 00:22:05.447
No, I don't think so.

00:22:12.290 --> 00:22:13.347
Madison...

00:22:13.690 --> 00:22:15.597
When were you mugged?

00:22:17.280 --> 00:22:19.207
Please, it's important, all right?

00:22:19.210 --> 00:22:20.647
Just answer the question.

00:22:24.590 --> 00:22:26.567
About a month ago.

00:22:26.570 --> 00:22:28.397
Did you see the guy? No.

00:22:28.400 --> 00:22:29.747
He grabbed me from behind.

00:22:29.750 --> 00:22:31.327
Did he bite you?

00:22:35.490 --> 00:22:37.377
How did you know that?

00:22:38.490 --> 00:22:39.787
Where?

00:22:39.790 --> 00:22:41.897
O-On the back of my neck.

00:22:51.940 --> 00:22:53.477
Oh, that's just a love bite.

00:22:53.480 --> 00:22:55.977
Believe me, that could
have been a lot worse.

00:22:56.620 --> 00:22:59.817
Where were you at the time?
Walking home from a friend's loft.

00:22:59.820 --> 00:23:00.757
Let me guess.

00:23:01.270 --> 00:23:03.477
Not too far from hunter's point?

00:23:07.060 --> 00:23:09.227
Same place where those
other murders happened.

00:23:09.230 --> 00:23:11.677
I'm telling you, it's the
werewolf's hunting grounds.

00:23:13.060 --> 00:23:15.117
But that doesn't mean it's
gonna be out there tonight.

00:23:15.120 --> 00:23:16.827
It's the right time of the lunar cycle.

00:23:17.590 --> 00:23:19.647
I know it's a long shot.

00:23:19.650 --> 00:23:20.737
You're forgetting something.

00:23:20.740 --> 00:23:22.077
Maddie's probably gonna turn soon.

00:23:22.080 --> 00:23:24.557
We can't let her take off
to an all-You-Can-Eat buffet.

00:23:25.470 --> 00:23:26.727
I'll stay with her.

00:23:26.730 --> 00:23:28.327
And if she busts loose?

00:23:30.170 --> 00:23:31.681
Sam? I'll do it.

00:23:32.190 --> 00:23:34.717
Sam. I'll shoot her, all right?

00:23:35.530 --> 00:23:37.697
But, dean, I need you to go out there.

00:23:37.740 --> 00:23:39.177
At least go look for the thing.

00:23:39.180 --> 00:23:40.377
Dean, please.

00:23:40.380 --> 00:23:42.137
We can save this girl.

00:23:45.910 --> 00:23:47.197
Fine.

00:23:54.380 --> 00:23:55.987
Please.

00:23:57.420 --> 00:23:59.307
Just let me go.

00:24:24.150 --> 00:24:25.327
Look...

00:24:26.920 --> 00:24:29.117
I know you're scared.

00:24:29.120 --> 00:24:32.377
I also know that there's no way
in hell you're gonna believe me.

00:24:33.560 --> 00:24:35.517
But I'm doing this...

00:24:36.480 --> 00:24:38.957
Because I'm trying to help you.

00:24:40.070 --> 00:24:41.270
I'm not gonna lie, all right?

00:24:41.273 --> 00:24:43.757
The odds aren't exactly in our favor.

00:24:44.250 --> 00:24:49.467
But if this goes the
way I pray it does...

00:24:50.010 --> 00:24:51.535
I'll untie you,

00:24:52.459 --> 00:24:56.067
And I'll walk out that door,
and I'll never come back.

00:24:57.230 --> 00:24:59.607
You'll live the rest of your life...

00:25:02.750 --> 00:25:06.247
And I'll just be a bad memory.

00:26:21.940 --> 00:26:22.657
Hey!

00:27:04.890 --> 00:27:06.447
It happened...

00:27:06.450 --> 00:27:08.127
Again.

00:27:08.950 --> 00:27:10.527
Where am I?

00:27:11.360 --> 00:27:13.507
H-Help me.

00:27:14.320 --> 00:27:16.667
God. Oh, my god.

00:27:16.670 --> 00:27:19.637
Easy gelen just take it easy

00:27:49.720 --> 00:27:51.407
It should be over now.

00:27:54.220 --> 00:27:56.347
You'll never see me again.

00:28:20.360 --> 00:28:22.197
It was sort of sad, actually.

00:28:22.610 --> 00:28:24.857
Glenn had no clue what was going on.

00:28:27.380 --> 00:28:30.497
Why do you think he turned Madison
instead of just killing her?

00:28:30.500 --> 00:28:31.807
I don't know.

00:28:31.810 --> 00:28:34.017
He kind of seemed to
have a thing for her.

00:28:34.020 --> 00:28:36.487
Maybe his primal instinct did, too.

00:28:37.530 --> 00:28:41.077
Maybe he was looking for a
little hot breeding action.

00:28:41.080 --> 00:28:42.787
Yeah. Something like that.

00:28:43.690 --> 00:28:44.977
So?

00:28:46.140 --> 00:28:47.117
So what?

00:28:47.120 --> 00:28:48.797
Speaking of madison... oh, whatever.

00:28:48.800 --> 00:28:51.757
You liked her. Maybe, uh
- Dean.

00:28:51.760 --> 00:28:53.832
She thought I was a
stark-Raving lunatic.

00:28:53.835 --> 00:28:54.593
You saved her life.

00:28:54.596 --> 00:28:56.547
But she doesn't know that.

00:28:57.510 --> 00:29:01.137
You know, for a stakeout,
your car's a bit conspicous.

00:29:01.454 --> 00:29:02.637
What are you still doing here?

00:29:02.640 --> 00:29:03.687
Honestly? Uh...

00:29:05.370 --> 00:29:07.433
We're pretty sure you're
not gonna turn tonight,

00:29:07.436 --> 00:29:09.859
But we got to be 100%,

00:29:09.862 --> 00:29:12.457
So, you know, we're... lurking.

00:29:14.490 --> 00:29:17.137
Look, I know this sounds crazy
- It sure does.

00:29:18.990 --> 00:29:21.187
Well, if we're gonna wait it out...

00:29:21.450 --> 00:29:23.697
We might as well do it together.

00:29:32.520 --> 00:29:34.737
You were telling the truth, weren't you?

00:29:34.740 --> 00:29:36.907
About everything.

00:29:38.860 --> 00:29:41.997
What you did -It was to help me.

00:29:42.600 --> 00:29:43.867
Yeah.

00:29:43.870 --> 00:29:46.317
I did all those horrible things...

00:29:47.580 --> 00:29:49.527
When I turned.

00:29:51.180 --> 00:29:52.757
You didn't know.

00:30:01.240 --> 00:30:03.857
So when will we know for sure?

00:30:03.860 --> 00:30:05.817
Moonrise?  No, I don't think so.

00:30:05.820 --> 00:30:07.027
You turned middle of
the night last night.

00:30:07.030 --> 00:30:09.337
I think we got to hang in until sunup.

00:30:16.860 --> 00:30:19.877
Well, looks like we got
ourselves a few hours to kill.

00:30:20.230 --> 00:30:21.837
Poker, anyone?

00:30:45.720 --> 00:30:47.027
Oh, no, you guys talk.

00:31:03.250 --> 00:31:05.567
Does -Does this mean it worked?

00:31:05.570 --> 00:31:07.267
Yeah, I think so.

00:31:09.040 --> 00:31:11.527
Oh, god, thank you.

00:31:11.530 --> 00:31:14.407
Thank you so much.

00:31:20.030 --> 00:31:22.227
You too, Dean.

00:31:22.230 --> 00:31:23.617
Thank you.

00:31:23.620 --> 00:31:25.527
Ah, don't mention it.

00:31:29.450 --> 00:31:37.667
So, I'm just gonna head back to the hotel
and watch some pay-Per-View or something.

00:31:45.180 --> 00:31:46.897
That was smooth.

00:31:47.710 --> 00:31:49.727
He means well.

00:31:49.730 --> 00:31:53.177
He means he thinks
you're gonna get laid.

00:31:54.680 --> 00:31:56.567
Look, I --
It's okay.

00:31:56.570 --> 00:31:57.727
No.

00:31:57.730 --> 00:32:00.087
I know I scared the crap
out of you, all right?

00:32:01.240 --> 00:32:02.837
I -I mean, I tied you to a chair.

00:32:02.840 --> 00:32:06.837
That's right up there with
me scratching up your face.

00:32:09.440 --> 00:32:11.587
There's just no way...

00:32:12.270 --> 00:32:14.427
We could go back, you know?

00:32:15.680 --> 00:32:17.537
To before it happened.

00:32:17.540 --> 00:32:18.757
You're right.

00:32:19.750 --> 00:32:22.027
There's just no way.

00:34:15.970 --> 00:34:17.917
She -She turned.

00:34:17.920 --> 00:34:18.907
What?

00:34:18.910 --> 00:34:21.087
I couldn't grab her in time.

00:34:21.480 --> 00:34:23.037
We'll find her, sammy.

00:34:23.040 --> 00:34:24.657
I already called bobby.

00:34:24.660 --> 00:34:28.267
He doesn't know anything, except he knew
severing the bloodline wouldn't work.

00:34:28.270 --> 00:34:30.687
They all say it's
impossible to reverse it.

00:34:30.690 --> 00:34:32.807
How come she didn't turn
when we were with her?

00:34:32.810 --> 00:34:34.498
You put her to bed and
then she wolfed out.

00:34:34.501 --> 00:34:35.817
Maybe she's got to be asleep to turn.

00:34:35.820 --> 00:34:37.177
What the hell does it matter?

00:34:37.180 --> 00:34:39.767
We got to find some way to
help her, some legend we missed.

00:34:39.770 --> 00:34:41.537
Don't you think someone
we know would have known?

00:34:41.540 --> 00:34:44.247
Then we have to look harder
until we find something.

00:34:44.590 --> 00:34:47.497
Sammy, I don't think we
got a choice here anymore.

00:34:48.950 --> 00:34:49.697
What?

00:34:49.700 --> 00:34:52.107
She's a sweet girl, but part of her is
- Evil?

00:34:52.110 --> 00:34:52.737
Yeah.

00:34:52.740 --> 00:34:54.567
That's what they say about me, dean.

00:34:54.570 --> 00:34:58.007
So me you won't kill, but her
you're just gonna blow away?

00:35:00.490 --> 00:35:01.757
Sam?

00:35:01.760 --> 00:35:03.207
Madison, where are you?

00:35:03.210 --> 00:35:05.787
I don't -I don't -I
don't know where I am.

00:35:06.170 --> 00:35:07.817
Do you see any street signs?

00:35:07.820 --> 00:35:10.027
Um... yeah, yeah.

00:35:10.030 --> 00:35:11.517
Middle point.

00:35:11.520 --> 00:35:12.407
Hold on, maddie.

00:35:12.410 --> 00:35:14.597
We're coming to get you.
Just stay where you are.

00:35:26.850 --> 00:35:29.837
I don't remember anything.

00:35:31.560 --> 00:35:34.347
I probably killed someone last night.

00:35:35.440 --> 00:35:36.877
Didn't I?

00:35:39.740 --> 00:35:41.567
There's no way to know yet.

00:35:41.570 --> 00:35:44.407
Is there something else we
can try to make it go away?

00:35:44.410 --> 00:35:45.637
We'll find something.

00:35:45.640 --> 00:35:48.657
There's got to be
some answer -Somewhere.

00:35:48.660 --> 00:35:50.387
That's not entirely true.

00:35:50.390 --> 00:35:52.387
Madison, you deserve to know.

00:35:53.550 --> 00:35:55.757
We've scoured every source.

00:35:56.470 --> 00:35:58.227
There's just no cure.

00:36:00.550 --> 00:36:02.237
Is -Is he right?

00:36:15.620 --> 00:36:18.567
Well, we could lock
you up at night, but...

00:36:18.570 --> 00:36:21.087
You bust out, and some night you will...

00:36:22.000 --> 00:36:23.947
Someone else dies.

00:36:27.620 --> 00:36:29.987
I'm sorry. I am.

00:36:38.170 --> 00:36:41.337
So I guess that's all
there is to it, then.

00:36:42.550 --> 00:36:44.357
Stop it. Don't talk like that.

00:36:44.360 --> 00:36:46.567
Sam, I don't want to hurt anyone else.

00:36:46.570 --> 00:36:48.617
I don't want to hurt you.

00:36:56.120 --> 00:36:57.527
Put that down.

00:36:57.530 --> 00:36:59.857
I can't do it myself.

00:37:02.600 --> 00:37:05.787
I need you to help me.  Madison, no.

00:37:05.790 --> 00:37:06.797
Sam.

00:37:07.080 --> 00:37:10.037
I'm a monster. You don't have to be.

00:37:10.800 --> 00:37:13.367
We could find a way, all right?

00:37:13.370 --> 00:37:15.367
I can. I'm gonna save you.

00:37:15.370 --> 00:37:16.957
You tried.

00:37:16.960 --> 00:37:18.817
I know you tried.

00:37:19.170 --> 00:37:21.797
This is all there is left.

00:37:22.230 --> 00:37:23.957
Help me, sam.

00:37:25.110 --> 00:37:27.287
I want you to do it.

00:37:28.420 --> 00:37:30.717
I want it to be you. I can't.

00:37:30.720 --> 00:37:32.987
I don't want to die.

00:37:32.990 --> 00:37:34.747
I don't.

00:37:35.260 --> 00:37:37.937
But I can't live like this.

00:37:40.020 --> 00:37:42.697
This is the way you can save me.

00:37:44.320 --> 00:37:46.487
Please.

00:37:47.960 --> 00:37:50.947
I'm asking you to save me.

00:38:45.950 --> 00:38:47.527
Sam

00:38:56.230 --> 00:38:57.287
I'm sorry.

00:38:57.290 --> 00:38:58.867
No, you're right.

00:39:00.170 --> 00:39:02.407
She's right.

00:39:03.690 --> 00:39:05.467
Sammy, I got this one. I'll do it.

00:39:05.470 --> 00:39:07.487
She asked me to.

00:39:08.460 --> 00:39:11.517
You don't have to. Yes, I do.

00:39:16.530 --> 00:39:18.387
Please.

00:39:27.730 --> 00:39:29.967
Just wait here.



00:00:15.500 --> 00:00:17.000
